{% extends 'legal/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Terms · {{ site.name }}{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Terms of use for {{ site.domain }}.{% endblock %}

{% block doc_title %}Terms of use{% endblock %}
{% block doc_subtitle %}Version {{ version }}. These terms cover the website at {{ site.domain }}.{% endblock %}

{% block doc_body %}
    <h2>1. Who runs the site</h2>
    <p>
        {{ site.name }} ({{ site.domain }}) is run by <strong>{{ site.operator }}</strong>
        ("we"). Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What the site is</h2>
    <p>
        A community calendar of urban kiz events in Europe: festivals, weekenders,
        workshops, parties and recurring socials. Listings are submitted by the
        people who run them or attend them and are checked by us before they are
        published. The site is free to use and free to list on.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Listings are information, not a promise</h2>
    <p>
        We check that a listing looks genuine before publishing it. We do not verify
        dates, prices, line-ups or venues with the organiser, and events change. Before
        you travel or buy a ticket, confirm the details with the organiser. We are not
        a party to any ticket sale and are not responsible for an event being cancelled,
        moved or different from its listing.
    </p>
    <p>
        A recurring social shows the date somebody last confirmed it was still running.
        Treat an old date as exactly that.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Submitting a listing</h2>
    <p>By submitting a listing you confirm that:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>the information is accurate to the best of your knowledge;</li>
        <li>you have the right to use any poster or image you upload, and grant us a
            non-exclusive licence to display it on the site, in the newsletter and in
            links to the listing shared on social media;</li>
        <li>the listing is for an urban kiz or closely related dance event in Europe,
            and is not advertising for anything else.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We may edit a listing for clarity (a city spelling, a missing country), decline
        it, or remove it at any time, and we do not have to give a reason. Rejected
        listings are visible to the person who submitted them, with a note where we
        left one.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Accounts</h2>
    <p>
        An account is an email address. You sign in with a one-time code we send to it;
        there is no password. Keep your inbox secure, because anyone who can read it
        can sign in as you. You can ask us to delete your account at any time by
        emailing <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>; listings you
        submitted stay on the site unless you ask for those to go too.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
        The newsletter goes only to addresses that have confirmed by clicking the link
        we send. Every issue carries an unsubscribe link, which works immediately and
        without signing in.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
        Do not submit listings that are false, that you do not have the right to post,
        or that are not what the site is for. Do not scrape the site at a rate that
        affects other visitors. We may block accounts or addresses that do.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Liability</h2>
    <p>
        The site is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we accept no
        liability for loss arising from reliance on a listing, from the site being
        unavailable, or from anything a third party does with information they found
        here. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes</h2>
    <p>
        We may change these terms. The version date at the top is the way to tell.
        Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the new terms.
    </p>
{% endblock %}

{% block doc_footer %}
    Version {{ version }}. Questions to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="underline">{{ site.email }}</a>.
{% endblock %}
